# Uploads. Nothing a user or a test run puts here belongs in the repository.
#
# This used to name one directory -- media/design_library/ -- while stating the
# intent for all of them, and the gap showed: sixteen files under media/ were
# tracked, including two customer-scoped fabric photographs under
# media/fabrics/cust_<uuid>/ and images uploaded through the customer profile
# form. Those are a boutique's clients' pictures, committed to a git remote.
#
# So the rule is inverted: everything under media/ is ignored, and the handful
# of seeded catalogue images the application genuinely ships with are named back
# in. `media/*` rather than `media/` is load-bearing -- git does not descend into
# an excluded directory, so the un-ignore lines below would never be consulted.
#
# Adding a new seeded image means adding it here. That is the point: it makes
# committing an upload a deliberate act rather than the default.
media/*
!media/design_ai_*.jpg
!media/design_cat_*.jpg
!media/fabric_*.jpg

